{
  "nodes": [
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier","label":"CGAN Learned run001 Fig1: Matched-Detectability Frontier","file_type":"image","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_matched_detectability_frontier","label":"Matched-Detectability Frontier (BER reachable vs P(detect) budget)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Five-panel step-curve figure: x = P(detect) budget for one specific detector (0 to 1), y = most BER reachable within that budget on a log axis from 1e-6 to 1e0. Faint dots are raw sweep points; the step curve is the running upper envelope, so each jammer is compared at matched detectability rather than matched configuration. Learned rows are evaluated on a 4 dB JSR grid."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_panel_power_one_sided","label":"Panel: Power Detector (1-sided)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Leftmost panel. Every jammer sits on the 1e-6 BER floor until a P(detect) budget of roughly 0.8; the shaped beta=0 learned curve is first off the floor at ~0.82 reaching ~2e-5, and all curves spike vertically only as the budget approaches 1.0, where matched QPSK reaches ~0.4 BER."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_panel_power_two_sided","label":"Panel: Power Detector (2-sided)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Second panel. Strictly harder for the jammers than the 1-sided power test: the floor is held until a budget of ~0.9, and all departures are compressed into the last tenth of the budget axis. The two-sided test catches power deficits as well as excesses, so a jammer cannot hide by reducing received power."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_panel_kurtosis","label":"Panel: Kurtosis Detector","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Middle panel and the weakest detector in the suite. Matched QPSK jumps to ~0.4 BER at a budget of only ~0.08, i.e. it is essentially invisible to a kurtosis test because same-modulation jamming does not change the fourth-moment statistic. Shaped beta=0 and pulsed p=0.1 also climb gradually from ~0.1 budget upward, unlike in the other panels."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_panel_spectrogram_cnn","label":"Panel: Spectrogram CNN Detector","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Fourth panel. The learned spectrogram detector suppresses noise, matched QPSK and the shaped jammers to the floor until ~0.6 budget, but the pulsed p=0.1 jammer escapes from ~0.38 budget and climbs smoothly to ~4e-2 BER, the clearest single-jammer weakness of the CNN: short duty-cycle bursts dilute the time-frequency evidence per frame."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_panel_noise_lrt_mismatched","label":"Panel: Noise LRT (mismatched)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Rightmost panel and the strongest detector shown: every jammer is pinned to the 1e-6 BER floor across the entire budget axis, with only a needle at budget 1.0 where the barrage-noise curve reaches ~0.2. Labelled 'mismatched' because the likelihood-ratio test is built for a Gaussian-noise jammer law and is applied to jammers that do not follow it, yet still dominates."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_far_alpha_budget","label":"FAR alpha = 0.05 Stealth Budget","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Dotted vertical reference at x = 0.05 in every panel: the detector's own false-alarm rate on clean frames, the project's definition of the stealth budget. Plotted in all five panels so the reader can read each frontier at the operationally meaningful budget rather than at a loose threshold such as P(det) <= 0.5."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_ber_floor","label":"BER Floor 1e-6 (no errors measured)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"The y-axis label states 1e-6 = no errors: the bottom of the log axis is a censoring floor standing in for zero measured bit errors, not a measured BER. Curves resting on it mean the jammer did no measurable damage at that budget."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_jammer_noise_barrage","label":"Jammer: Noise (barrage)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Light-blue baseline series: Gaussian barrage jamming. Stays on the BER floor in every panel except for a spike at budget ~1.0, i.e. it is only effective once it is certain to be detected."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_jammer_matched_qpsk","label":"Jammer: Matched QPSK (p=1)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Orange baseline series, full duty cycle: Zhou's same-modulation 'optimal' jammer. The most effective jammer in the figure (~0.4 BER) but only cheaply so against kurtosis; against power, CNN and noise-LRT it needs a near-unity detection budget."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_jammer_pulsed","label":"Jammer: Pulsed p=0.1","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Pink series, 10% duty cycle. The only jammer that trades gracefully against the spectrogram CNN, producing a long smooth staircase from ~0.38 budget to ~4e-2 BER instead of an all-or-nothing vertical jump."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_jammer_shaped_beta0","label":"Jammer: Shaped, beta=0 (learned)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Black series: the learned shaped jammer with no stealth weight, i.e. trained for damage alone. Reaches ~1.5e-3 BER but only from mid-to-high detection budgets; it is the first learned curve off the floor in the power panels (~0.82)."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_jammer_shaped_beta001","label":"Jammer: Shaped, trained vs this detector, beta=0.01","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Dashed dark-blue series: shaped jammer trained against the detector of its own panel with a small stealth weight beta=0.01 in the BER - beta*detections reward. Rises almost vertically at a budget of ~0.9 to 0.95 in every panel, so the small stealth weight did not buy a low-budget operating point."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_jammer_shaped_beta1","label":"Jammer: Shaped, trained vs this detector, beta=1","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Solid dark-blue series: same detector-aware training with a heavy stealth weight beta=1. Tracks the beta=0.01 curve closely and also only departs the floor near budget 1.0, which is the figure's evidence that raising beta did not move the frontier left."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_finding_kurtosis_blind_to_matched_modulation","label":"Finding: Kurtosis is Blind to Matched-Modulation Jamming","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Matched QPSK reaches near-maximal BER (~0.4) at a kurtosis budget of ~0.08, two to three orders of magnitude cheaper in detectability than against any other detector in the suite. A same-modulation jammer leaves the fourth standardised moment of the received samples essentially unchanged, so the statistic has nothing to key on."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_finding_pulsed_evades_cnn","label":"Finding: Pulsed Duty Cycle is the Spectrogram CNN's Weak Axis","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"In the Spectrogram CNN panel the pulsed p=0.1 jammer dominates every other jammer, including the detector-aware learned ones, over the whole budget range 0.38 to 1.0. A hand-designed duty-cycle jammer beating jammers trained against that exact detector suggests the learned attacker under-explored the temporal axis."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_finding_no_damage_at_far_budget","label":"Finding: No Jammer Does Damage at the FAR Stealth Budget","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"At the dotted alpha = 0.05 line every curve in all five panels rests on the 1e-6 no-errors floor. The frontier is empty at the operationally meaningful stealth budget, so the headline must be reported as a negative result for this run rather than as a stealth/effectiveness trade-off."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_finding_detector_aware_training_no_gain","label":"Finding: Detector-Aware Training Did Not Move the Frontier Left","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"Both beta=0.01 and beta=1 shaped jammers, trained against the detector of their own panel, depart the BER floor only at budgets of ~0.9 or higher, at or to the right of the detector-agnostic beta=0 curve. Adding the stealth term to the BER - beta*detections reward bought no low-budget damage at either weight."},
    {"id":"artifacts_cgan_learned_run001_fig1_frontier_finding_lrt_dominates_suite","label":"Finding: Mismatched Noise LRT Still Dominates the Detector Suite","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/home/rrahman/BT/Tabula Rasa/artifacts/cgan/learned/run001/fig1_frontier.png","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,
      "rationale":"The Noise LRT panel is flat on the floor across the whole budget axis while all four other detectors admit some damage, so a likelihood-ratio test built for the wrong jammer law is still the hardest detector to beat. Consistent with the project's P_NP >= P_learned >= P_energy invariant carried over from m0/detectors.py."}
  ],
